;; L, the Cistern's lower half. The chute from K lands on the west ledge
;; (row 5), whose east lip (3) is worn and gives way; two glide hops east
;; over the fissure pits (4-tile gaps, 2 rows down): the ledge (8-9) and the
;; floor beyond (14-), which
;; runs east into M, the Last Step (rows 8-9). A miss lands in the pits (x)
;; and the soft return puts you back on the ledge you left.
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (7 7)
  title: "The Cistern"
  intent: "the old people's cistern, dry now, its worn ledges stepping down across a fissure into the dark"
  bed: (hum 0.8 air 0.7 water 0.2)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("#  ######################"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "####                    #"
   "###                     #"
   "###     ##               "
   "###xxxxxxxxxxx           "
   "#########################")
  things: ((thin-ice at: (3 6)))
  decor: none)
